---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CtaBand from '../../../components/CtaBand.astro';

const categories = [
  {
    id: 'gorilla',
    label: 'Gorilla Trekking',
    icon: 'M12 2C6.48 2 2 6.48 2 12s4.48 10 10 10 10-4.48 10-10S17.52 2 12 2zm-2 15l-5-5 1.41-1.41L10 14.17l7.59-7.59L19 8l-9 9z',
    faqs: [
      { q: 'How much does a Uganda gorilla trekking permit cost?', a: 'A Uganda gorilla trekking permit costs USD 800 per person for foreign non-residents. Foreign residents pay USD 700, and East African citizens pay USD 80. The permit covers your park entry fee, a Uganda Wildlife Authority ranger guide, and 24-hour armed security. During low season (April, May, November) the permit drops to USD 600 for foreign non-residents.' },
      { q: 'Is seeing gorillas guaranteed?', a: 'Yes. The Uganda Wildlife Authority habituates gorilla families specifically for tourism. Your ranger tracks the family the morning of your trek using GPS data from the previous evening. Sightings are not legally guaranteed, but the success rate is consistently above 99%. Bwindi has 19 habituated families available for visitors.' },
      { q: 'How far in advance should I book a gorilla permit?', a: 'Book at least 3 to 6 months in advance, especially for the peak dry seasons: June to September and December to February. Permits are limited to 8 visitors per gorilla family per day and the most popular families sell out quickly. Once you confirm your date with us we arrange all logistics around it.' },
      { q: 'What is the minimum age for gorilla trekking?', a: 'The minimum age is 15 years, set by the Uganda Wildlife Authority. This protects the gorillas from childhood illnesses and ensures all participants can meet the physical demands. Children under 15 cannot trek even with a paid permit, and no refund is issued. There is no upper age limit; seniors trek regularly with the option of a porter-carried sedan chair.' },
      { q: 'How long does gorilla trekking take?', a: 'Trekking time varies from 30 minutes to 8 hours depending on where the gorilla family moved overnight. The average is 2 to 4 hours through the forest. Once you locate the gorillas you get exactly 1 hour with them. The total day, including lodge transfer, briefing and trekking, typically takes 6 to 9 hours.' },
      { q: 'How physically difficult is gorilla trekking?', a: 'Trekking ranges from moderate to strenuous. Trails pass through dense rainforest on steep, often muddy slopes at 1,500m to 2,500m altitude. You should be comfortable walking for several hours on uneven terrain. Porters are available at the trailhead for USD 15 to 20 and carry your daypack while assisting on difficult sections. Walking sticks are provided free of charge.' },
      { q: 'What are the rules during a gorilla trek?', a: 'Uganda Wildlife Authority rules: maintain at least 7 metres from the gorillas; no flash photography; no eating, drinking or smoking in their presence; voices low at all times; do not trek if you have a cold, flu or any transmissible illness; maximum 8 people per family per day; the 1-hour limit is strictly enforced. These rules protect the gorillas and ensure the experience remains available for future visitors.' },
      { q: 'What is the gorilla habituation experience?', a: 'The Gorilla Habituation Experience is available in the Rushaga sector of Bwindi. It allows 4 hours with a family that is still being accustomed to human presence, at a cost of USD 1,500 per person. This is ideal for photographers and serious wildlife enthusiasts who want extended time with the gorillas rather than the standard 1-hour encounter.' },
    ]
  },
  {
    id: 'planning',
    label: 'Planning Your Safari',
    icon: 'M17 12h-5v5h5v-5zM16 1v2H8V1H6v2H5c-1.11 0-1.99.9-1.99 2L3 19c0 1.1.89 2 2 2h14c1.1 0 2-.9 2-2V5c0-1.1-.9-2-2-2h-1V1h-2zm3 18H5V8h14v11z',
    faqs: [
      { q: 'What is the best time to visit Uganda?', a: 'Uganda can be visited year-round; gorilla trekking is possible in every month. The best conditions are during the two dry seasons: June to September and December to February. Trails are drier and forest walks are easier. The wet seasons (March to May and October to November) bring lush green landscapes, fewer crowds and discounted permit prices, but trails are muddier. Even in the wet season, rain usually falls in short afternoon bursts.' },
      { q: 'How many days do I need for a Uganda safari?', a: 'A minimum of 3 days covers a single activity such as gorilla trekking or Murchison Falls. For a complete Uganda experience including gorilla trekking, chimpanzee tracking, a game drive and a boat cruise, plan for 7 to 10 days. Our most popular itinerary is 7 days covering Bwindi, Kibale Forest and Queen Elizabeth National Park. Combining Uganda with Kenya or Rwanda needs 10 to 14 days.' },
      { q: 'Is Uganda safe for tourists?', a: 'Yes. Uganda is one of the safest countries in East Africa for travelers. National parks are well-patrolled by Uganda Wildlife Authority rangers. Standard travel awareness applies: keep valuables out of sight, use recommended transport providers and follow your guide at all times. All L\'okawa tours include experienced local guides who know the terrain and ensure your safety throughout.' },
      { q: 'Do I need a visa to visit Uganda?', a: 'Most nationalities require a visa, available online via the Uganda e-Visa portal before travel. The standard tourist visa costs USD 50 and covers a single entry for 90 days. The East Africa Tourist Visa (USD 100) grants entry to Uganda, Rwanda and Kenya on one permit, excellent value for multi-country trips. Apply at least 2 weeks before travel. Contact us with your nationality and we will advise on the exact requirements.' },
      { q: 'What vaccinations do I need?', a: 'Yellow Fever vaccination is mandatory for entry into Uganda; carry your Yellow Card certificate. Recommended vaccinations include Hepatitis A and B, Typhoid, Tetanus and Meningococcal Meningitis. Malaria prophylaxis is strongly recommended for all visitors. Consult your GP or travel health clinic at least 4 to 6 weeks before departure. Bring DEET-based insect repellent and wear long-sleeved clothing in the evenings.' },
      { q: 'Uganda vs Rwanda: which is better for gorilla trekking?', a: 'Both are excellent but suit different traveler profiles. Uganda (USD 800 permit) offers better value, more habituated families (19 vs 12 in Rwanda), and the option to combine gorillas with chimp tracking and game drives. Rwanda (USD 1,500 permit) has shorter treks to the gorillas, more polished luxury lodge options and a well-developed tourism infrastructure. Most budget-conscious first-timers choose Uganda; returning travelers or those wanting luxury tend to prefer Rwanda.' },
    ]
  },
  {
    id: 'booking',
    label: 'Booking & Payments',
    icon: 'M20 4H4c-1.11 0-2 .89-2 2v12c0 1.11.89 2 2 2h16c1.11 0 2-.89 2-2V6c0-1.11-.89-2-2-2zm0 14H4v-6h16v6zm0-10H4V6h16v2z',
    faqs: [
      { q: 'How do I book a safari with L\'okawa Tours?', a: 'Send an enquiry via our Contact page or WhatsApp (+256 761 512 966) with your preferred dates, number of travelers and the destinations you are interested in. We respond within 24 hours with a tailored itinerary and quote. Once you are happy with the proposal, a 30% deposit confirms the booking and we immediately secure your gorilla permits and accommodation. The balance is due 30 days before your arrival date.' },
      { q: 'What deposit is required to confirm a booking?', a: 'A 30% deposit of the total tour cost confirms your safari. This covers the gorilla and chimpanzee permits, which must be paid in full to the Uganda Wildlife Authority at the time of booking and are non-refundable. The remaining 70% is due 30 days before departure. For last-minute bookings made within 30 days of travel, full payment is required at the time of booking.' },
      { q: 'What payment methods do you accept?', a: 'We accept international bank transfer (USD preferred), Western Union and mobile money for clients in Uganda. Bank transfer details are provided with your booking confirmation. All tour prices are quoted in US Dollars. Bank transfer fees are the responsibility of the client.' },
      { q: 'What is the cancellation policy?', a: 'Cancellations more than 60 days before departure incur a 30% fee. Cancellations between 30 and 60 days before departure incur a 50% fee. Cancellations within 30 days of departure are non-refundable. Gorilla and chimpanzee permits are always non-refundable once purchased from Uganda Wildlife Authority. We strongly recommend comprehensive travel insurance that covers safari cancellation.' },
      { q: 'What is included in the tour price?', a: 'All L\'okawa packages include: all meals as specified in the itinerary, private 4x4 safari vehicle with roof hatch, park entrance fees, English-speaking professional driver-guide, bottled drinking water, and boat cruise fees where listed. Gorilla and chimpanzee permits are included where those activities appear in the itinerary. Excluded: international flights, visa fees, travel insurance, alcohol, laundry, tips (recommended USD 10 to 15 per day) and optional activities.' },
      { q: 'Do you offer custom safari packages?', a: 'Yes, the majority of our safaris are tailored to each client\'s dates, budget, group size and interests. If no package matches what you want, contact us and we will design a bespoke itinerary across Uganda, Kenya, Tanzania and Rwanda. We can add gorilla habituation, specialist birding guides, community walks and more. There is no extra charge for custom planning.' },
    ]
  },
  {
    id: 'packing',
    label: 'Packing & Preparation',
    icon: 'M20 6h-2.18c.07-.44.18-.88.18-1 0-2.21-1.79-4-4-4s-4 1.79-4 4c0 .12.11.56.18 1H8c-1.1 0-2 .9-2 2v12c0 1.1.9 2 2 2h12c1.1 0 2-.9 2-2V8c0-1.1-.9-2-2-2zm-6-3c1.1 0 2 .9 2 2s-.9 2-2 2-2-.9-2-2 .9-2 2-2zm0 13l-4-4 1.41-1.41L14 13.17l5.59-5.59L21 9l-7 7z',
    faqs: [
      { q: 'What should I wear for gorilla trekking?', a: 'Wear long-sleeved shirts and long trousers in neutral or khaki colours. Long sleeves protect against stinging nettles and insects. Sturdy waterproof hiking boots with ankle support are essential on steep, muddy terrain. Bring thick garden gloves to grip vegetation, a lightweight rain jacket and gaiters to keep mud out of your boots. Avoid bright colours, camouflage and strongly scented products.' },
      { q: 'What should I pack for an East Africa safari?', a: 'Pack light; most safari vehicles and light aircraft have a 15kg luggage limit. Essentials: neutral safari clothes (2 to 3 outfits), a warm fleece for early morning game drives, wide-brimmed hat, high-SPF sunscreen, DEET insect repellent, personal medications, small first-aid kit, quality camera, binoculars, phone with offline maps, universal power adapter and sufficient USD cash for tips and purchases.' },
      { q: 'Do I need travel insurance?', a: 'Yes. We require all clients to have valid comprehensive travel insurance before the safari begins. Your policy should cover emergency medical evacuation (critical in remote areas), trip cancellation and curtailment, loss of pre-paid permits, baggage loss and personal liability. Safari-specific adventure travel policies are available from providers such as World Nomads or Battleface. Traveling without adequate insurance is a serious risk.' },
      { q: 'Is it safe to drink the water in Uganda?', a: 'Do not drink tap water. All L\'okawa safari vehicles carry unlimited bottled water throughout your tour. Lodges and camps provide boiled or filtered water. Brush your teeth with bottled water. Check the seal when buying water in towns. Avoid ice in drinks at basic restaurants. Fruit you peel yourself such as bananas and oranges is generally safe. We brief all clients on food and water safety before departure.' },
    ]
  },
];

const schema = JSON.stringify({
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": categories.flatMap(cat =>
    cat.faqs.map(f => ({
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": f.q,
      "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": f.a }
    }))
  )
});
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Gorilla Trekking & Safari FAQ | L'okawa Tours Uganda"
  description="Answers to the most common questions about Uganda gorilla trekking permits, safari costs, packing, safety, best time to visit and booking with L'okawa Tours."
  schema={schema}
>

<!-- ════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     PAGE BANNER
════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div class="faq-banner">
  <svg viewBox="0 0 1440 340" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMax slice" class="faq-banner__svg" aria-hidden="true">
    <circle cx="1130" cy="230" r="110" fill="#ffd45a" opacity=".2"/>
    <circle cx="1130" cy="230" r="72"  fill="#ffd45a"/>
    <path d="M0 270 C220 240 400 266 580 244 C780 220 940 262 1140 242 C1280 228 1370 250 1440 244 L1440 340 L0 340Z" fill="#1d3315" opacity=".8"/>
    <path d="M0 304 C240 282 440 304 660 292 C880 280 1100 306 1440 286 L1440 340 L0 340Z" fill="#0d1a0a"/>
    <g fill="#0d1a0a">
      <rect x="1246" y="206" width="9" height="90"/>
      <ellipse cx="1250" cy="200" rx="86" ry="22"/>
      <ellipse cx="1196" cy="214" rx="50" ry="14"/>
      <ellipse cx="1306" cy="212" rx="50" ry="14"/>
    </g>
  </svg>
  <div class="faq-banner__overlay" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="faq-banner__content">
    <div class="faq-banner__breadcrumb">
      <a href="/" class="faq-banner__bc-link">Home</a>
      <span>&nbsp;/&nbsp;</span>
      <span class="faq-banner__bc-cur">FAQs</span>
    </div>
    <p class="faq-banner__kicker">Before you book</p>
    <h1 class="faq-banner__h1">Safari &amp; Gorilla<br class="faq-banner__br"/> Trekking FAQ</h1>
    <p class="faq-banner__sub">Everything you need to know about permits, costs, packing and what to expect on your East Africa adventure.</p>
    <div class="faq-cats">
      {categories.map(cat => (
        <a href={`#${cat.id}`} class="faq-cat-pill">{cat.label}</a>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     FAQ BODY — two-column layout
════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div class="faq-body">
  <div class="container faq-layout">

    <!-- Sticky sidebar nav -->
    <aside class="faq-sidebar">
      <p class="faq-sidebar__label">Jump to section</p>
      <nav>
        {categories.map(cat => (
          <a href={`#${cat.id}`} class="faq-sidebar__link">
            <span class="faq-sidebar__dot"></span>
            {cat.label}
          </a>
        ))}
      </nav>
      <div class="faq-sidebar__cta">
        <p class="faq-sidebar__cta-text">Still have a question?</p>
        <a href="/contact/" class="btn btn--primary" style="width:100%;text-align:center;">Contact Us</a>
        <a href="https://wa.me/256761512966" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="faq-sidebar__wa">
          <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M17.472 14.382c-.297-.149-1.758-.867-2.03-.967-.273-.099-.471-.148-.67.15-.197.297-.767.966-.94 1.164-.173.199-.347.223-.644.075-.297-.15-1.255-.463-2.39-1.475-.883-.788-1.48-1.761-1.653-2.059-.173-.297-.018-.458.13-.606.134-.133.298-.347.446-.52.149-.174.198-.298.298-.497.099-.198.05-.371-.025-.52-.075-.149-.669-1.612-.916-2.207-.242-.579-.487-.5-.669-.51-.173-.008-.371-.01-.57-.01-.198 0-.52.074-.792.372-.272.297-1.04 1.016-1.04 2.479 0 1.462 1.065 2.875 1.213 3.074.149.198 2.096 3.2 5.077 4.487.709.306 1.262.489 1.694.625.712.227 1.36.195 1.871.118.571-.085 1.758-.719 2.006-1.413.248-.694.248-1.289.173-1.413-.074-.124-.272-.198-.57-.347m-5.421 7.403h-.004a9.87 9.87 0 0 1-5.031-1.378l-.361-.214-3.741.982.998-3.648-.235-.374a9.86 9.86 0 0 1-1.51-5.26c.001-5.45 4.436-9.884 9.888-9.884 2.64 0 5.122 1.03 6.988 2.898a9.825 9.825 0 0 1 2.893 6.994c-.003 5.45-4.437 9.884-9.885 9.884m8.413-18.297A11.815 11.815 0 0 0 12.05 0C5.495 0 .16 5.335.157 11.892c0 2.096.547 4.142 1.588 5.945L.057 24l6.305-1.654a11.882 11.882 0 0 0 5.683 1.448h.005c6.554 0 11.89-5.335 11.893-11.893a11.821 11.821 0 0 0-3.48-8.413z"/></svg>
          WhatsApp us
        </a>
      </div>
    </aside>

    <!-- Main accordion content -->
    <main class="faq-main">
      {categories.map(cat => (
        <section id={cat.id} class="faq-section">
          <div class="faq-section__head">
            <div class="faq-section__icon">
              <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="var(--color-amber)" aria-hidden="true">
                <path d={cat.icon}/>
              </svg>
            </div>
            <h2 class="faq-section__title">{cat.label}</h2>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-list">
            {cat.faqs.map(item => (
              <details class="faq-item" name={`faq-${cat.id}`}>
                <summary class="faq-item__q">
                  <span>{item.q}</span>
                  <svg class="faq-item__chevron" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
                    <polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/>
                  </svg>
                </summary>
                <div class="faq-item__a"><p>{item.a}</p></div>
              </details>
            ))}
          </div>
        </section>
      ))}
    </main>

  </div>
</div>

<!-- ════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     BOTTOM CTA BAND
════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<CtaBand
  heading="Ready to plan your safari?"
  btn1="Get a Free Quote"
  btn1Href="/contact/"
  btn2="View Safari Packages"
  btn2Href="/tours/"
/>

</BaseLayout>

<style>
/* ════════════════════════════════════════
   PAGE BANNER
════════════════════════════════════════ */
.faq-banner {
  position: relative;
  overflow: hidden;
  min-height: 340px;
  background: linear-gradient(180deg, #16290f 0%, #2f4d20 40%, #b8561a 82%, #f4b41a 100%);
}
.faq-banner::before {
  content: '';
  position: absolute;
  inset: 0;
  background-image: url('/images/gorillas/baby-gorilla-closeup.jpg');
  background-size: cover;
  background-position: center 30%;
  opacity: 0.22;
  z-index: 0;
}
.faq-banner__svg {
  position: absolute; left: 0; bottom: 0;
  width: 100%; height: 100%;
  pointer-events: none; z-index: 1;
}
.faq-banner__overlay {
  position: absolute; inset: 0;
  background: linear-gradient(90deg,
    rgba(10,20,8,.82) 0%, rgba(10,20,8,.45) 55%, rgba(10,20,8,0) 85%);
  z-index: 1;
}
.faq-banner__content {
  position: relative; z-index: 2;
  max-width: var(--max-width);
  margin-inline: auto;
  padding: 70px var(--section-pad-x) 100px;
  box-sizing: border-box;
}
.faq-banner__breadcrumb {
  font-size: 14px; font-weight: var(--weight-semibold);
  letter-spacing: .06em; color: var(--color-cream); margin-bottom: 14px;
}
.faq-banner__bc-link { color: var(--color-cream); transition: color var(--transition-fast); }
.faq-banner__bc-link:hover { color: var(--color-gold); }
.faq-banner__bc-cur { color: var(--color-gold); }
.faq-banner__kicker {
  font-family: var(--font-display); font-style: italic;
  font-weight: 500; font-size: 22px;
  color: var(--color-gold); margin-bottom: 6px; display: block;
}
.faq-banner__h1 {
  font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: var(--weight-bold);
  font-size: 64px; line-height: var(--leading-tight);
  color: var(--color-white); margin: 0 0 14px;
}
.faq-banner__br { display: block; }
.faq-banner__sub {
  font-size: var(--text-lg); color: var(--color-cream);
  line-height: var(--leading-relaxed); max-width: 520px;
  margin-bottom: 28px; opacity: .9;
}

/* Category pills */
.faq-cats { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 10px; }
.faq-cat-pill {
  background: rgba(255,255,255,.12);
  color: var(--color-cream);
  border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.25);
  border-radius: var(--radius-full);
  padding: 8px 18px;
  font-size: var(--text-sm); font-weight: var(--weight-bold);
  letter-spacing: var(--tracking-wide); text-transform: uppercase;
  transition: background var(--transition-fast), border-color var(--transition-fast), color var(--transition-fast);
}
.faq-cat-pill:hover {
  background: var(--color-amber); border-color: var(--color-amber);
  color: var(--color-forest-deep);
}

/* ════════════════════════════════════════
   TWO-COLUMN LAYOUT
════════════════════════════════════════ */
.faq-body { padding: 72px 0 80px; background: var(--color-bg); }
.faq-layout {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 240px 1fr;
  gap: 48px;
  align-items: start;
}

/* ════════════════════════════════════════
   SIDEBAR
════════════════════════════════════════ */
.faq-sidebar {
  position: sticky;
  top: 100px;
  background: var(--color-white);
  border-radius: var(--radius-xl);
  padding: 24px;
  box-shadow: var(--shadow-card);
}
.faq-sidebar__label {
  font-size: var(--text-xs); font-weight: var(--weight-extrabold);
  letter-spacing: var(--tracking-widest); text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--color-text-muted); margin-bottom: 14px;
}
.faq-sidebar__link {
  display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px;
  padding: 9px 10px; border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
  font-size: var(--text-sm); font-weight: var(--weight-semibold);
  color: var(--color-text-body);
  transition: background var(--transition-fast), color var(--transition-fast);
  border-left: 3px solid transparent;
}
.faq-sidebar__link:hover {
  background: var(--color-parchment);
  color: var(--color-forest);
  border-left-color: var(--color-amber);
}
.faq-sidebar__dot {
  width: 7px; height: 7px; border-radius: 50%;
  background: var(--color-card-border); flex-shrink: 0;
  transition: background var(--transition-fast);
}
.faq-sidebar__link:hover .faq-sidebar__dot { background: var(--color-amber); }
.faq-sidebar__cta {
  margin-top: 24px; padding-top: 20px;
  border-top: 1px solid var(--color-card-border);
  display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;
}
.faq-sidebar__cta-text {
  font-size: var(--text-sm); font-weight: var(--weight-bold);
  color: var(--color-forest); margin-bottom: 2px;
}
.faq-sidebar__wa {
  display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; gap: 8px;
  background: #25D366; color: #0b2b14;
  border-radius: var(--radius-lg); padding: 10px 14px;
  font-size: var(--text-sm); font-weight: var(--weight-extrabold);
  transition: opacity var(--transition-fast);
}
.faq-sidebar__wa:hover { opacity: .88; }

/* ════════════════════════════════════════
   ACCORDION SECTIONS
════════════════════════════════════════ */
.faq-section {
  margin-bottom: 56px;
  scroll-margin-top: 100px;
}
.faq-section:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
.faq-section__head {
  display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 14px;
  margin-bottom: 20px; padding-bottom: 16px;
  border-bottom: 2px solid var(--color-card-border);
}
.faq-section__icon {
  width: 44px; height: 44px; border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
  background: var(--color-parchment);
  display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
  flex-shrink: 0;
}
.faq-section__title {
  font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: var(--weight-bold);
  font-size: var(--text-3xl); color: var(--color-forest);
}
.faq-list { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 3px; }
.faq-item {
  border: 1px solid var(--color-card-border);
  border-radius: var(--radius-lg); overflow: hidden;
  background: var(--color-white);
  transition: border-color var(--transition-fast);
}
.faq-item[open] { border-color: var(--color-amber); }
.faq-item__q {
  display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center;
  gap: 16px; padding: 18px 22px;
  font-weight: var(--weight-bold); font-size: var(--text-base);
  color: var(--color-forest); cursor: pointer; list-style: none;
  transition: background var(--transition-fast);
  line-height: var(--leading-normal);
}
.faq-item__q::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
.faq-item__q:hover { background: var(--color-parchment); }
.faq-item[open] .faq-item__q {
  background: var(--color-parchment); color: var(--color-amber);
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-card-border);
}
.faq-item__chevron {
  flex-shrink: 0; color: var(--color-amber);
  transition: transform var(--transition-base);
}
.faq-item[open] .faq-item__chevron { transform: rotate(180deg); }
